<article class="env-lemma" id="067K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/067K">Lemma <span data-tag="067K">15.84.5</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a finite type ring map with $A$ a regular ring of finite dimension. Then $A \to B$ is perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00OE" data-tag="00OE">10.110.8</a> the assumption on $A$ means that $A$ has finite global dimension. Hence every module has finite tor dimension, see Lemma <a href="/tag/066P" data-tag="066P">15.68.19</a>, in particular $B$ does. By Lemma <a href="/tag/067I" data-tag="067I">15.84.3</a> the map is pseudo-coherent. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>